  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and Solutions for Afghan refugees, asylum seekers, host communities and stateless persons in Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the stark reality of the Afghan refugees entering a third generation of exile and the current fluid situation in Afghanistan, the operation is focused on improving the prospects for realizing solutions. Voluntary return remains the main solution for most refugees if conditions permit. Cognizant of the economic challenges for sustainable reintegration in Afghanistan, a reinforced approach to livelihoods has been made with a core component being to enable voluntary returns for skilled refugees. Cross-border mechanisms to systematically link skilled refugees with employment options in the priority areas of return and reintegration (PARRs) in Afghanistan continue to be strengthened towards this end. Efforts to include refugees within Afghan peace and stabilization processes are also being put in place. Alongside these efforts, the organisation is exploring options for complementary pathways and meeting increased resettlement quotas.</narrative>
  </description>
